{
  "what": "The stereo gate on the nine ElevenLabs cues of 2026-10-10: measured, and the eight that failed it narrowed in mid/side (driver item 53e; finding PR-0425 of deep review round 24, build 72973096, which measured boss-bahamut and boss-leblanc)",
  "words": "i'll go with all your recommendations even as to music and sound effects. you recommend an dchoose it please. this is extremely important. (Bailey, 2026-10-10 23:05 EDT); the driver chose to fix the gate by measurement, not to stage a wide-versus-narrow listening choice",
  "gameCase": "FFX-2: boss-bahamut (Chapter IV), boss-leblanc (Chapter VI and the hidden Leblanc chapter), boss-ffx2-fallen-aeons (Chapters XI and XVI), boss-trema (Chapter XIII phase 2). FFX: boss-seymour-natus (X), boss-isaaru (XIV), boss-sin-assault (XVII), boss-sin-countdown (XVIII). FF7: boss-ff7-guard (the hidden limit chapter), which passed already and is unchanged. Each cue plays only where its own record says; the fix changes the stereo image of the file and nothing a chapter routes to.",
  "gate": {
    "thresholds": {
      "corr": [
        0.6,
        0.85
      ],
      "sideMid": [
        -10,
        -6
      ],
      "monoLossMin": -1
    },
    "source": "THEMES.md \"Since 2026-10-07 (ElevenLabs)\"; GATES in tools/audio/remaster-score.mjs",
    "measuredWith": "tools/audio/stereo-gate.mjs, on the decoded MP3 (ffmpeg, 44.1 kHz stereo float, whole file): L/R Pearson correlation, side-to-mid 10 log10(mean S^2 / mean M^2) with S = (L-R)/2 and M = (L+R)/2, mono-sum loss 10 log10(mean M^2 / mean channel power). The round-24 auditor's script (critic/rounds/round-24/stereo-gate.mjs) gives the same figures: boss-bahamut 0.408, -3.72, -1.54 and boss-leblanc 0.257, -2.28, -2.02 were reproduced to the digit before anything was changed."
  },
  "method": {
    "tool": "tools/audio/stereo-narrow.mjs",
    "what": "Mid/side: M = (L+R)/2 is kept, S = (L-R)/2 is multiplied by one broadband gain below 1, L = M+gS, R = M-gS. It is instantaneous, so nothing moves in time: the length, the loop points and the 3 s run-on are the input's sample for sample (lag 0 against the original at 10 %, 50 % and the end of every file; the same frame count and gapless-header delay and padding). Then one linear gain to -16 LUFS (ffmpeg ebur128, as the lane pipelines measured it) and LAME V4 (-q:a 4), the encode the lanes used. The decoded MP3 is what is measured, and the side gain and the master gain are iterated until the encode reads side-to-mid -7.5 dB and -16.0 LUFS.",
    "target": "side-to-mid -7.5 dB, which is correlation 0.70 and mono-sum loss -0.70 dB (all three follow from the side/mid power ratio r: corr = (1-r)/(1+r), loss = -10 log10(1+r)); the middle of the correlation and side windows, 1.5 dB from the nearest edge",
    "source": "the shipped MP3, decoded once (no WAV or other lossless master exists: the lanes' masters are LAME V4 MP3s and the raw takes are 128 to 320 kbps MP3s); the loop crossfade and the run-on are built into it",
    "limiter": "boss-sin-countdown only: the master gain (+2.1 dB) took its true peak to -0.47 dBTP, over the -1 dBTP gate, so a look-ahead limiter (the lane pipelines' own, 10 ms) at -1.7 dBFS acts on 13 samples, by at most 0.63 dB; the other seven needed none",
    "reproduce": "node tools/audio/stereo-narrow.mjs --in=<dir of the pre-fix files> --out=<dir> --cue=<the eight> --install; then node tools/audio/stereo-gate.mjs <cue> ..."
  },
  "wideFiles": {
    "where": "git 5c371dcd (public/audio/music/<cue>.mp3 at the r40 release candidate before this change) and D:/Tools/pyrefly-scratch/2026-10-10/stereo-53e/wide; each cue's `before.sha256` names its file",
    "restore": "git show 5c371dcd:public/audio/music/<cue>.mp3 > public/audio/music/<cue>.mp3, then put that cue's `before.manifestEntry` back in the manifest and the older record's `file` and `manifestEntry` (its `laneFile`)"
  },
  "notMeasured": "Nobody has heard these files (AGENTS.md rule 13). The gate is a measurement and Bailey's ear can overrule it: the narrow files are less wide than the takes he was offered, and he may prefer the wide ones (the D-582 class of question).",
